 ## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
 
+The model is instructed to distinguish saved edits from verified results and to report blocked, interrupted, skipped, and failing checks explicitly. These instructions guide generated summaries; they do not certify task completion. For Node tests blocked by child-process EPERM, an in-sandbox `--test-isolation=none` run is an option only when isolation is not required. Its result must identify the changed test mode and leave the original command unverified; rejected escalation cannot be bypassed this way.
+
